ion baseline using perturbation identity\\\",\\n          \\\"scVI / scVI-LD conditional variational autoencoders\\\",\\n          \\\"scGen latent space vector arithmetic with out-of-distribution perturbation prediction\\\",\\n          \\\"CPA (Compositional Perturbation Autoencoder)\\\",\\n          \\\"GEARS graph neural network with gene co-expression and gene ontology priors\\\",\\n          \\\"PerturbNet conditional generative model with normalizing flows\\\",\\n          \\\"SAMS-VAE sparsity-aware variational autoencoder\\\",\\n          \\\"scGPT / Geneformer / scBERT transformer-based single-cell foundation models\\\",\\n          \\\"scFoundation multiscale transformer for single-cell expression\\\",\\n          \\\"CellForge-style conditional autoencoder for CRISPR perturbation prediction\\\"\\n        ],\\n        \\\"strengths\\\": [\\n          \\\"Latent variable models capture cell-to-cell heterogeneity and stochasticity in scRNA-seq\\\",\\n          \\\"Conditional autoencoders such as CPA are explicitly designed for unseen perturbation prediction\\\",\\n          \\\"Graph neural network approaches leverage gene-gene interactions and biological priors\\\",\\n          \\\"Foundation models can transfer representations from large single-cell corpora\\\",\\n          \\\"Several methods provide uncertainty estimates for predicted perturbation responses\\\",\\n          \\\"Linear baselines are interpretable, fast, and robust to small training sample sizes\\\"\\n        ],\\n        \\\"limitations\\\": [\\n          \\\"Unseen CRISPRi perturbations often have sparse effects, and whole-transcriptome MSE is dominated by unchanged genes\\\",\\n          \\\"CRISPRi off-targets, variable knockdown efficiency, and clone effects confound training signals\\\",\\n          \\\"Deep latent models may require many training perturbations and can overfit to strong effects\\\",\\n          \\\"Black-box models lack mechanistic interpretability for downstream b